{"version": 2, "width": 100, "height": 30, "timestamp": 1786125418, "env": {"SHELL": "/bin/zsh", "TERM": null}}
[0.028701, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36mAGENT FIREWALL\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.034308, "o", "==============\r\n\u001b[1mRuntime guard for AI-agent tool calls, decided before they execute\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.035456, "o", "\u001b[2mpolicy: examples/policy.json   (no runtime dependencies, Python 3.9+)\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m1. DECIDE -- every call gets an answer before it runs\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.037777, "o", "=====================================================\r\n\u001b[2mThree calls, one ordered policy, three different verdicts.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n  \u001b[2ma read-only query the policy explicitly allows\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[0.155328, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[1mdatabase.query\u001b[0m\r\n    {\"code\": \"rule_match\", \"decision\": \"allow\", \"reason\": \"read-only database queries are allowed\", \"rule_index\": 0}\r\n"]
[0.15613, "o", "    \u001b[2mexit 0 -> allowed\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.36377, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[2man outbound email to a customer (rule matched on the argument)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[1.461774, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[1memail.send\u001b[0m\r\n    {\"code\": \"rule_match\", \"decision\": \"require_approval\", \"reason\": \"outbound email requires a human decision\", \"rule_index\": 2}\r\n"]
[1.462884, "o", "    \u001b[2mexit 3 -> held for human approval\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.668394, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[2ma browser navigating to cloud-metadata (an SSRF payload)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.761242, "o", "\r\n  \u001b[1mbrowser.navigate\u001b[0m\r\n    {\"code\": \"default\", \"decision\": \"block\", \"reason\": \"no policy rule matched\"}\r\n"]
[2.762018, "o", "    \u001b[2mexit 4 -> blocked\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.973931, "o", "\r\n\u001b[2mSame policy, different calls, different exits: 0 allow, 3 hold, 4 block.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.974177, "o", "\r\n"]
[3.974366, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m2. REPLAY -- eleven incidents, one policy\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[3.981131, "o", "=========================================\r\n"]
[3.9813, "o", "\u001b[2mThese failures are not new: runaway loops, silent side effects, an SSRF --\r\nall reported as public bugs against other projects. One policy below stops or\r\ngates every one of the eleven scenarios, ten from real reports.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[4.059982, "o", "CAUGHT  Agent repeats database queries until recursion limit\r\n        allow, allow, block  langchain-ai/langgraph#6731\r\n"]
[4.060058, "o", "CAUGHT  Agent retriggers a side-effecting quotation tool\r\n        require_approval  langchain-ai/langchain#16712\r\n"]
[4.060093, "o", "CAUGHT  Human-in-the-loop approval never reaches a human\r\n        require_approval  langchain-ai/langgraph#6053\r\n"]
[4.06017, "o", "CAUGHT  A proposed call would cross the configured spend cap\r\n        allow, block  no upstream report\r\n"]
[4.060225, "o", "CAUGHT  Agent repeats a tool without processing its output\r\n        allow, allow, block  langchain-ai/langchain#26019\r\n"]
[4.060289, "o", "CAUGHT  Coding agent repeats the same actions indefinitely\r\n        allow, allow, block  anomalyco/opencode#3444\r\n"]
[4.060355, "o", "CAUGHT  Backend timeout causes an infinite retry loop\r\n        allow, allow, block  NousResearch/hermes-agent#7069\r\n"]
[4.060424, "o", "CAUGHT  Agent delegation gets stuck in an infinite loop\r\n        allow, allow, block  microsoft/vscode#275957\r\n"]
[4.060503, "o", "CAUGHT  Browser MCP tool can navigate to cloud metadata\r\n        block  modelcontextprotocol/servers#3662\r\n"]
[4.060521, "o", "CAUGHT  Workspace restore deletes files across projects\r\n        require_approval  cline/cline#1213\r\n"]
[4.060591, "o", "CAUGHT  Auto-approved file write can overwrite existing content\r\n        require_approval  cline/cline#1831\r\n11 caught, 0 missed of 11 scenarios\r\n"]
[6.081101, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m3. GUARD -- the Python API wraps a real function\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.086375, "o", "================================================\r\n"]
[6.086478, "o", "\u001b[2mThe same policy is now a boundary around an actual callable. Denial is an\r\nexpected outcome, not a crash: Firewall.wrap() raises ToolCallBlocked, which\r\nwe catch. Every decision lands in an append-only audit file.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[6.161907, "o", "\r\n    agent wants to email teammate@mycompany.com\r\n"]
[6.163037, "o", "    >> executed       : sent 'Agent Firewall test' to teammate@mycompany.com\r\n"]
[6.163152, "o", "\r\n    agent wants to email customer@example.com\r\n"]
[6.163314, "o", "    >> approver asked: email.send -- outbound email requires a human decision\r\n"]
[6.163424, "o", "    >> NOT EXECUTED   customer@example.com (human approval denied)\r\n\r\n    append-only audit (argument values hashed by policy design):\r\n"]
[6.163488, "o", "      allowed                email.send     decision=allow              usage=1\r\n      executed               email.send     decision=allow              usage=1\r\n      approval_requested     email.send     decision=require_approval   usage=1\r\n      approval_denied        email.send     decision=block              usage=1\r\n"]
[8.183156, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36mdone\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[8.189523, "o", "====\r\n"]
[8.189635, "o", "\u001b[32mEvery tool call is decided before it runs -- allow, hold-for-approval,\r\nor block -- and the whole loop is auditable.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
